            "description": {
              "content": "This API endpoint retrieves a list of all pipeline executions that have been triggered by a specific schedule in a Bitbucket repository. By providing the workspace identifier, repository slug, and schedule UUID in the path, users can view the historical execution records for that particular scheduled pipeline. This is useful for monitoring and auditing purposes, allowing teams to track when scheduled pipelines have run, verify their execution history, and identify any patterns or issues with automated pipeline triggers. The endpoint returns execution details that help developers understand how their scheduled CI/CD processes are performing over time.",
